 "notes": "Catalog.API only (the one service with a committed spec); v1 and v2 specs merged because the code serves both versions. The 4 v1 routes the extractor misses all carry route constraints the path literal check rejects: {name:minlength(1)}, {text:minlength(1)}, {brandId?}, {brandId:int?} (category route-constraint-syntax). Calls: every outbound call in the client service folders, written with the prefix the code itself holds (class field / const); the host comes from AddHttpClient BaseAddress (config, linker's job). The prefix \"api/catalog/\" lives in a field interpolated into the URL and is dropped as a base placeholder (field-in-interpolation, wrong per H2-D12). HybridApp repeats the WebAppComponents calls with ?api-version=2.0 in the literal, which makes the template rejected (query-in-template): none extracted. Paths kept as the code writes them (catalogBrands vs catalogbrands) — ASP.NET routing is case-insensitive, which is the linker's concern. Routes: 20 of 23 sampled (seed 1). Identity.API's AccountController uses conventional routing ({controller}/{action}); its [HttpGet]/[HttpPost] without a template come out as GET / and POST / (route-by-name-convention) and the controller's five actions collapse into those two. Recall extended by hand to Ordering.API/Apis/OrdersApi.cs and Webhooks.API/Apis/WebHooksApi.cs: group roots MapGet(\"/\") / MapPost(\"/\") are dropped (root-route-dropped) and MapGet(\"{orderId:int}\") has no leading slash (no-leading-slash). Not in a scope: MapMethods(\"/check\", [HttpMethods.Options]) comes out as ANY — the collection-expression method list is not read. 2026-10-15: the two AccountController items left the sample — the extractor no longer emits a template-less action of a controller without [Route] (they were the sample's only wrong routes). 2026-10-15 (second round): the calls list missed GET /api/webhooks (WebHooksClient.cs:12, GetFromJsonAsync<IEnumerable<...>>) — the grep used to list the calls skipped nested generics, the same reason the extractor did; added. With the query string and .TrimEnd accepted and nested generics read, the catalog calls of WebAppComponents and HybridApp are all extracted now, still without the \"api/catalog/\" of the interpolated field (field-in-interpolation).",
